      "output": {
        "message": "Here are three low-pressure ways to start shifting that routine: 1. **Pick a consistent \"third place.\"** Choose one spot outside of home and work—like a neighborhood café, library, climbing gym, or park—and go at the same time once or twice a week. Becoming a familiar face is often the easiest way casual interactions start naturally.\n2. **Find an activity with built-in interaction.** Look for local meetups centered on something you already like doing, such as a casual run club, a board game night, a rec sports league, or a volunteer shift. Shared activities take the awkwardness out of small talk because there’s already an objective.\n3. **Plan an evening out on your own.** You don’t have to wait for company to leave the apartment. Taking a book to a diner, catching a movie, or exploring a new neighborhood gets you out into the city’s energy without the pressure to socialize immediately. See if any of those fits the kind of energy you have right now, and start with just one evening this week.",
